{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/684305-court-system-idea-the-courts-of-morr-god-of-death-and-dreams","id":684305,"title":"(Court System Idea) The Courts of Morr, God of Death And Dreams","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-01T05:44:33-07:00","id":684305,"title":"(Court System Idea) The Courts of Morr, God of Death And Dreams","content":"Does that name not sound familiar? If not, you're far from the only one. Morr is actually entirely fictional, one of ye old venerable Warhammer Fantasy Battles pantheon before it was the Sigmar and Chaos Show,all the time (I blame 40K, and the fact that setting was originally intended as a fun, not-at-all-serious splinter of Warhammer Fantasy). As the name implies, he's the relatively kindly God of the Dead, and Sleep in general, with a bit of a side job as a patron of prophets.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was reading up on old material, and I realized Morr has a lot of similarities to another semi-benign figure known to changelings, the Pale Brother (Dancers in Dusk-he's an aspect of the Grim Reaper who appears in dreams, normally people's dying ones but he's known to guest star in dreams about accepting death). So, I say to myself-let's say some British changeling, recently escaped and still massively confused over what the world really is, happens to meet the Pale Brother, and being a Warhammer fan, decides that Morr is real (or at least inspired by a real god)?<br /> <br /> What happens next is that he founds a Court set dedicated to Morr as a whole, with each individual taking after his wife Verena (goddess of truth and justice-also known for supporting debates into what those concepts really are), and daughters Shallya (mercy and healing) and Myrmidia (strategic warfare). And Ranald (trickster god of luck and thieves), because according to cosmology a changeling needs both a great deal of luck and larcenist ability to break the unclean law of the True Fae and get back to Earth, so not letting Ranald have his say is incredibly stupid. <br /> <br /> Naturally, their Bulwark causes the Huntsmen to take after Chaos Daemons and undead, which Morr hates (with the exception of ghosts, which are held to be so wrapped up in the pain of their deaths they cannot make the Final Pilgrimage to Morr's Kingdom of Sleep-and even then it's held that you're supposed to help them move on). <br /> <br /> So good genesis of an idea? I'll post the Contract ideas and what emotions they focus on later, when I finally get another part of this project I have out of the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-01-2015, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:11:27-07:00","id":684350,"title":"","content":"Interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:45:32-07:00","id":684372,"title":"","content":"Is each deity getting their own Court, or is this paradigm just one Court?<br /> Also, not to be nit-picky as I don't actually know but isn't it Approaches that define how Huntsmen appear? Thus the Court Approach forces them into the roll of Choas Daemons or Undead...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:54:30-07:00","id":684578,"title":"","content":"Each deity gets their own court, with regular tribute to Morr.<br /> <br /> And the Approaches meaning that the Huntsmen look and act like Daemons and Undead was what I was implying, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T11:29:56-07:00","id":684675,"title":"","content":"Approaches don't define how a Huntsman looks-that's a little more complicated of a subject.<br /> <br /> But there's a little build to purpose in there, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"